  "id": "DrugBank_DB00563 - MONDO_4638",
  "verbalization": "Methotrexate is implicated in the progression of lymphosarcoma through a series of indirect pathways, primarily via the induction of temsirolimus and carmustine, both of which are indicated in lymphosarcoma. The evidence suggests that Methotrexate may act as a precursor in the treatment of certain lymphomas, such as B-cell neoplasm and non-Hodgkin lymphoma, leading to the activation of temsirolimus or carmustine, which in turn contribute to the development or progression of lymphosarcoma. This implies a potential role of Methotrexate in the pathogenesis of lymphosarcoma through the activation of downstream pathways involving temsirolimus and carmustine. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Methotrexate may influence lymphosarcoma, although the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
